.TH ENCODE-BENCH 1 "2026-10-10" "encode-bench" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
encode-bench \- VMAF calibration bench for ffmpeg-encode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B encode-bench
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B encode-bench
encodes short samples of real files with a baseline (HEVC CQP) and a sweep of
AV1 CQP qualities, scores each against the source with libvmaf, and reports
size vs quality so you can pick the AV1 quality matching current HEVC output.
.P
VMAF runs with
.I n_subsample
(default 5): scoring every frame buffers the whole stream and peaks at several
GB of RAM. It reuses
.B ffmpeg-encode
own command builder, so it measures the exact pipeline the TUI uses.
Requires
.BR ffmpeg (1)
with libvmaf and a VAAPI device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-seconds " SECONDS"
Sample length. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-\-offset " OFFSET"
Sample start offset. Default: 5.
.TP
.BI \-\-hevc\-quality " N"
HEVC baseline CQP quality. Default: 27.
.TP
.BI \-\-hevc\-values " N..."
Extra HEVC \-qp values to sweep.
.TP
.BI \-\-av1\-values " N..."
AV1 CQP \-global_quality values to sweep. Default:
.BR 90 " " 95 " " 97 " " 100 " " 105 .
.TP
.BI \-\-tolerance " N"
Allowed VMAF drop vs baseline. Default: 0.5.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
libvmaf threads. Default: half the CPUs.
.TP
.BI \-\-n\-subsample " N"
Score every Nth frame. Default: 5.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Keep encoded samples instead of deleting them.
.SH EXAMPLES
Calibrate AV1 against one file:
.IP
.EX
encode-bench ~/Videos/sample.mkv
.EE
.P
Sweep custom AV1 values, keep samples:
.IP
.EX
encode-bench \-\-av1\-values 95 100 110 \-\-keep clip.mkv
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed.
.TP
.B 1
No VAAPI device found, or a sample failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg-encode (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
